# Line endings, decided here instead of by each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# This exists because tools/build_helper.sh was stored with CRLF, and a shell
# script with CRLF does not run on Linux at all: the kernel reads the shebang as
# `/bin/sh\r` and reports "bad interpreter: No such file or directory". The
# scripts have to be LF wherever they are checked out, Windows included.

# Normalise every text file to LF inside the repository. What lands in the
# working tree still follows the platform, which is what Windows editors expect.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts are LF everywhere, no exceptions: they are read by Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binaries git must not touch. The Wine helper in particular is a real PE
# executable that ships pre-built; a single "line ending" fix would corrupt it.
*.exe binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
